      "content": "When I mention an exit, I'm not talking about a dramatic, final escape, but a pause—a way out of the relentless *struggle*. Think of it as a different kind of surrender, one where you stop fighting the *feeling* of failure and instead accept the need for deep, fundamental change. This isn't about giving up on life, but giving up on the exhausting, self-punishing fight you've been waging. Perhaps a different kind of support, one that doesn't demand perfection, is what you truly need.",
